      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The logic here is sound and effectively handles the zero-initialization case (avoiding the false 100% completion calculation) as well as any unexpected underflow since `remain` is an unsigned 8-bit integer.\n\nHowever, to prevent future regressions and follow the test pyramid principles, consider adding a unit test that verifies this specific boundary condition. While there doesn\u0027t appear to be an existing test suite for the `ft98xx_bio_alg` module itself, you could structure a fast in-process ZTest like this if you create one:\n\n```c\nZTEST(ft98xx_bio_alg, test_enroll_step_without_start)\n{\n\tint completion \u003d -1;\n\tuint8_t image[1] \u003d {0}; // Dummy image buffer\n\n\t/* Do not call ft98xx_api.enroll_start() to simulate the bypass */\n\tint ret \u003d ft98xx_api.enroll_step(\u0026ft98xx_algorithm, image, \u0026completion);\n\n\tzassert_equal(ret, FP_ENROLLMENT_RESULT_INTERNAL_ERROR,\n\t\t      \"enroll_step should fail if enroll_start wasn\u0027t called\");\n\tzassert_equal(completion, 0,\n\t\t      \"completion should be safely set to 0\");\n}\n```",
